{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/930733-what-are-your-shard-ideas","id":930733,"title":"What are your Shard ideas?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-07-12T23:35:18-07:00","id":930733,"title":"What are your Shard ideas?","content":"Shards are exactly what they sound like; little pieces of settings that break away from the core canon. CofD has had a few so far (generic cyberpunk and space opera, while Demon got a couple specific ones) and we know Scion 2e will eventually have some as well. Are there any ideas bursting out of your skulls?<br /> <br /> I'm just wrapping up a playthrough of Shin Megami Tensei IV, a game that [SPOILERS] largely takes place in a ruined Tokyo that God and Lucifer are fighting over (via mortal dupes and numerous angels and demons), and the sequel is about the various polytheistic pagan deities realising that they can carve out niches for themselves while the Abrahamic powers are distracted. Stealing that general idea and turning the Pantheons into feuding gangs struggling to steal turf and followers sounds like it could be an awesome chronicle of done right. You could either spin it as &quot;you're all drawn from one Pantheon and need to help it become top dog in the city&quot; or &quot;you're all from different Pantheons and need to convince people to focus on the greater thread/not murdering each other over petty shit,&quot; depending on what strikes your fancy more.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-13T01:34:00-07:00","id":930744,"title":"","content":"Crap. I never even considered doing shards. I mean, yeah, Ragnarok could be considered one and I've thought about giving each of the Pantheons a similar make over with their own end times, but I never considered Shards. Cyberpunk, Steampunk, basically lots of punks. 80's Horror, Far Flung Space Opera, Wild West, Roman Conquest. The list goes on and on and really sounds like a great game. WWII was interesting, but I think a Civil War game could be just as fun. Revolutionary War is a pretty obvious one. Basically any war would work. I find the SciFi ideas to be the most interesting though. I'm all about doing a game where either you play the old gods fighting the new gods or the new gods out trying to make a name for themselves. Both set in a Blade Runner setting would be amazing. Just some thoughts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1101-blindst","name":"blindST","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1101_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-13T05:20:10-07:00","id":930781,"title":"","content":"I proposed this idea before in the Games Like Scion thread, but I suppose it could work as a shard setting, too.<br /> <br /> Instead of the Scions trying to join their divine parents in the Overworld, they're planning to replace them at their jobs. Armageddon has arrived, and it's time to elect the creator gods of the next world. But with only so many positions to go around, this election takes the form of trial by combat.<br /> <br /> The shard could have elements from Highlander, or Baldur's Gate to it, in which the Scions are hunting down and killing each other to increase their chances of becoming the next generation of Gods.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-13T09:04:38-07:00","id":930889,"title":"","content":"Roger Zelazny's Amber universe is easily one of my favorites. I could never convince any of my friends to try the diceless version that was out. As far as video games went, the Final Fantasy series has tons of epicness to it and of course I'd love to do Star Wars, any era even if I lean towards the Old Republic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/333-achilles","name":"Achilles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar333_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-13T10:17:04-07:00","id":930920,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Achilles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/930733-what-are-your-shard-ideas?p=930889#post930889\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Roger Zelazny's Amber universe is easily one of my favorites. I could never convince any of my friends to try the diceless version that was out. As far as video games went, the Final Fantasy series has tons of epicness to it and of course I'd love to do Star Wars, any era even if I lean towards the Old Republic.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Oh definitely, Final Fantasy is a perfect fit for a shard! Especially since it combines Modern, Medieval, and Future settings all in one.<br /> <br /> Maybe the Life Stream could be converted into some kind of Underworld?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 07-13-2016, 01:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-13T12:11:53-07:00","id":930971,"title":"","content":"Hmmm Shadowrun strangely enough is another RPG that would mix well if you make a few mythological corrections, who says Ares and Lone Star can't be touched by ares, or Aztech actually have the blessing of several Aztec gods?<br /> <br /> I would love a setting set in some sort of Pangea where every civilization remains stationary in it's golden days. Sun Wukong kept traveling west and made trouble for Lugh. Odysseus definitely ran into Vikings on his way back home. A setting where history and geography doesn't really apply. Every group is at its height of power<br /> <br /> A world where the gods don't just exist on the fringes but openly believed to be real by everyone. Magazines talk about Zeus' latest lover. Decorators offer tips on how to set up a couple's shrines without angering the house spirits or their respective gods, and the latest sitcom is about a single parent raising a scion and their wacky shenanigans. (not realistic but it's comedy so real scions rarely mind). Everyone knows when the Pharaoh is born regardless of religion since it's a big event, and minor gods are accepted reality among the everyday.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11938-3comrades","name":"3Comrades","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"90"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-13T12:15:14-07:00","id":930972,"title":"","content":"In a strange twist of fate, the gods die from some disease/curse/what-have-you. The players then need to fill in the roles. As they increase in power, then those aspects also increase in the world. Should someone be a god of war, then there is more war. Fertility means more children and this overpopulation. So forth and so on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/786-thedonnie","name":"thedonnie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-13T12:16:23-07:00","id":930974,"title":"","content":"I might look at stealing the Better Angels campaign &quot;No Soul Left Behind.&quot; That game's normally about modern day people turned into supervillains by demons (in the case of that particular campaign, you play the staff and students of a failing inner city school), but I'm sure the rough outline should still work with Scion. <br /> <br /> I'm picturing a Scion of Zeus as a really hardcore PE teacher who wants his students to be worthy of the ancient Olympic games and it's funny enough to sell me on the entire concept.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-13T15:28:54-07:00","id":931043,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>3Comrades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/930733-what-are-your-shard-ideas?p=930971#post930971\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I would love a setting set in some sort of Pangea where every civilization remains stationary in it's golden days. Sun Wukong kept traveling west and made trouble for Lugh. Odysseus definitely ran into Vikings on his way back home. A setting where history and geography doesn't really apply. Every group is at its height of power</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Lionhead's series Black and White has a setting like that.<br /> <br /> The world of Eden is a place where ancient cultures from radically different time periods exist in the same era. So you have the ancient Greeks, the feudal Japanese, the Norse vikings, the Aztecs, Native Americans all living together. Well, I say living together, but it's more like they're trying to convert / rape and pillage one another because their Gods are trying to grab as much territory as possible.<br /> <br /> Except in the game, Gods are born from pure prayers (a mortal has an actual need for divine intervention) instead of natural reproduction. Which means instead of Gods creating mortals, the mortals created Gods.<br /> <br /> <br /> ------------------------------------------------<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/930733-what-are-your-shard-ideas?p=930974#post930974\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm picturing a Scion of Zeus as a really hardcore PE teacher who wants his students to be worthy of the ancient Olympic games and it's funny enough to sell me on the entire concept.</div> </div> </div> </div>Does he make them compete in the nude? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> ---------------------------------------------<br /> <br /> <br /> I would also like to see a shard based on the Elder Scrolls series, since the game's lore says that it is actually possible to become a God, and several mortals have managed to do so before. Mannimarco and Tiber Septim being two popular examples.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 07-13-2016, 06:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-13T20:44:58-07:00","id":931167,"title":"","content":"The Gods came to Earth once, millennia ago. They gave us many gifts, shaped our very civilizations, and then left for somewhere far, far away. In the very codes of our DNA, they left something even greater...<br /> <br /> Some few special humans in every generation claim a little of the power of the Gods. For centuries, they have been called Scions for each reflects the nature of a particular ancient deity. It is a matter of some rigorous debate whether Scions are actually descended from the Gods themselves, or is somehow chosen based on choices made in life. Do the children of Poseidon ache for the sea, or do great sailors earn his favor? Humanity has wrestled with these questions since time immemorial, but on the wings of its greatest scientific achievement, humanity is now ready to seek its greatest adventure.<br /> <br /> Thanks in no small part to the contributions of great Scion thinkers, humanity has finally conquered interstellar travel. Now courageous bands of Scions ply the unexplored infinity of the stars... seeking the Gods themselves. They find other worlds, more recently touched by the hands of the Gods, a trail of breadcrumbs leading into the unknown. Most remarkable of all, it seems that the nearer the Scions come to the distant homes of the Gods, the more Godlike they, themselves, become...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12108-gscrap","name":"gscrap","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12108_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-13T22:01:42-07:00","id":931186,"title":"","content":"Cronus dethroned his father Uranus and was in turn torn down by his son Zeus; it is the natural way of things for the young to violently eclipse the old when they achieve the power to do so. The gods of Olympus have hidden themselves from the world of man for ages now in order to avoid the turning of the cycle once more, but Fate cares not for their machinations and a new generation is born to begin the divine struggle anew. Can one band of Scions avoid destruction at their parents' hands long enough to usurp them?<br /> <br /> The game begins as a largely Scion story but with only one Pantheon (the Theoi) and a distinctly adversarial tone. As the band rises in power, the gods grow increasingly bold in hunting them as their desperation rises, culminating with the gods revealing themselves to humanity in exchange for the masses aid in killing their children.<br /> <br /> I'm toying with the idea of riffing off the recent trend of dystopian YA novels (wherein the protagonists stand out from the rest for whatever reason - in this case, divine birthright - and are nearly crushed as they work to dismantle things) as the framework for this, where the climax of the story is the band leading an armed rebellion against their holy parents. Maybe some of the gods see the writing on the wall and attempt to sell out their peers out in exchange for survival and a place in the new Pantheon, or even take an active role in trying to steal parts of the others' abilities; it could be fun to see poor Hephaestus attack Ares with the players' help, becoming murderous and vengeful in his own right.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-13T23:09:05-07:00","id":931207,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/930733-what-are-your-shard-ideas?p=931186#post931186\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The game begins as a largely Scion story but with only one Pantheon (the Theoi) and a distinctly adversarial tone. As the band rises in power, the gods grow increasingly bold in hunting them as their desperation rises, culminating with the gods revealing themselves to humanity in exchange for the masses aid in killing their children.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b>Plot Twist:</b> the Scions could turn mortals against the existing Theoi under the idea that they are outdated and barbaric, requiring humanity to put a more modernized pantheon into power.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-14T11:04:01-07:00","id":931466,"title":"","content":"<b>Mythic Age Shard:</b> Taking place in the time before recorded history, the players assume the roles of established pantheons when they were still young and inexperienced. The gods do not yet wield the power they are so famously known for, as players help them grow and mature into their roles.<br /> <br /> <br /> -----------------------------------<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Super Hero Shard:</b> Instead of going on crazy adventures, the Scions want to retain some resemblance of a normal life. Unfortunately, their Fateful Aura constantly makes this a problem for them. To compensate, the Scions dress up as alter egos to protect their identities while still fulfilling their Scion obligations.<br /> <br /> <br /> -------------------------------------<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Schoolyard Shard:</b> Instead of being scattered all over the world, Scions are gathered together in training academies designed to help them prepare for the war against the Titans. Shard would have elements of Percy Jackson, My Hero Academia, Super Hero High, and other popular high school action series.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-14T11:06:20-07:00","id":931467,"title":"","content":"Hmmmn hows this sound for a Shard? Axis Won WW2<br /> <br /> lets see what the repercussions there would be.<br /> <br /> In particular I could see collaborators from the Russian or French pantheons being aided in founding new puppet dynastys.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-15T13:42:56-07:00","id":932180,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/930733-what-are-your-shard-ideas?p=931466#post931466\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Mythic Age Shard:</b> Taking place in the time before recorded history, the players assume the roles of established pantheons when they were still young and inexperienced. The gods do not yet wield the power they are so famously known for, as players help them grow and mature into their roles.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would like to hear more about this one if you have anymore thought on it Nyrufa, sounds like something my players/I would be interested in using.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2295-coderr","name":"CodeRR","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2295_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-15T14:25:04-07:00","id":932207,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CodeRR</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/930733-what-are-your-shard-ideas?p=932180#post932180\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I would like to hear more about this one if you have anymore thought on it Nyrufa, sounds like something my players/I would be interested in using.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Sure. As an added twist, I would suggest that you use the <i>history is written by the victors</i> approach for acting out the legends. After all, we don't actually know how Zeus managed to defeat the Titans, we only know that he did so, and all we have to go by is his account on things.<br /> <br /> The truth could be that Zeus barely scraped by at times!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-16T10:52:04-07:00","id":932565,"title":"","content":"<b>Sci-Fi Shard:</b> Megaman-esque world where gods and scions are sophisticated androids, and the Titan of Chaos takes the form of a virus.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Fantasy Shard:</b> Taking place in the classical / middle ages of mankind, where Lesser Immortals and Titan Spawn lived openly among humans.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Wire Fu Action Shard:</b> An eastern concentrated setting where only the Asian pantheons are used.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>The Other Side Shard:</b> Flip the game's setting so you play as the children of Titans fighting to avenge their usurpation by the arrogant Gods. Gradually increasing your power until you come to embody a primordial concept, as well!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 07-16-2016, 01:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-17T07:40:00-07:00","id":932899,"title":"","content":"<b>The Expendables Shard:</b> In a world where <i>any deity</i> is capable of producing a Scion, you play the children of lesser immortals. Not as popularly recognized as the major pantheons, you are considered B-List cannon fodder in the war against the Titans.<br /> <br /> <i>Note:</i> Sort of a comedy-action setting in which we get to see how hard the little guys work to support the big stars in the Titan war.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Berserk Shard:</b> In a world where humanity is subjugated and tortured at the whims of immortals, you have a chance to rise above lesser men and take your place at the top of society. But be warned, the consequences for failing are infinitely worse than being a slave.<br /> <br /> <i>Note:</i> For those who haven't read / watched Berserk, be advised the setting deals with some pretty extreme themes including, but not limited to rape, hell, psychological trauma, religious fanaticism, human sacrifice, class warfare, gender inequality, and the inquisition itself!<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>It's all Wrong Shard:</b> The pantheons have been rewritten to fit the popular modern depictions of their mythology. Some Gods are better people because of it, and some are much, much worse!<br /> <br /> <i>Note:</i> An alternate setting in which we follow the bastardized interpretations of the classical mythology as told from a modern perspective.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-25T21:22:02-07:00","id":937465,"title":"","content":"<b>Shin Megami Tensei Shard:</b> An alternate take on the Titanomachy in which the Titans of Chaos and Order are at war with one another and everybody else is picking a side. As the players grow in power, they must decide whether to stand on the side of Chaos, Order, or fight for Independence from both.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-25T21:38:26-07:00","id":937468,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/930733-what-are-your-shard-ideas?p=937465#post937465\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Shin Megami Tensei Shard:</b> An alternate take on the Titanomachy in which the Titans of Chaos and Order are at war with one another and everybody else is picking a side. As the players grow in power, they must decide whether to stand on the side of Chaos, Order, or fight for Independence from both.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> SMTIV FINAL (or Apocalypse in the USA) paints a large number of pagan gods as making a move while YHVH and Lucifer are busy fighting each other, while The Dagda is trying to kill all gods.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-26T18:31:12-07:00","id":937855,"title":"","content":"<b>Rebel Alliance Shard:</b> The Overworld war is done, the Gods failed and humanity is once again subjugated under the rule of the Titans, as they were eons ago. But even though the Gods have fallen, there is still hope; there are still Scions! The lines between pantheons and cultures have been erased, and rather than squabbling among each other, the Scions have banded together under a singular army with the intention of succeeding where the Gods failed. Some say that without the aid of the Gods, the rebels are facing an uphill battle, but others believe that unifying the pantheons may be our one hope of victory in this post-apocalyptic scenario!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-27T06:09:07-07:00","id":938055,"title":"","content":"I'd love to explore the Darksider's universe as a scion of one of the Horsemen after a reboot of Creation or a Horseman in training going around and getting to know all these other realms.Obviously more exploratory than hack and slash.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/333-achilles","name":"Achilles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar333_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-27T12:04:24-07:00","id":938258,"title":"","content":"Zombies. The Gods and Titans have died, but their creations and Scions have been left behind, as the world descends into a post apocalyptic hell hole...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2783-tytalus","name":"Tytalus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2783_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"491"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-27T13:05:59-07:00","id":938289,"title":"","content":"I do think the first Shard we're gonna do is post-apocalyptic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-27T17:16:44-07:00","id":938441,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/930733-what-are-your-shard-ideas?p=938289#post938289\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do think the first Shard we're gonna do is post-apocalyptic.</div> </div> </div> </div>do you think the gods would be stronger weaker or the same in a post-apocalyptic World?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-27T20:01:21-07:00","id":938532,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/930733-what-are-your-shard-ideas?p=938441#post938441\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">do you think the gods would be stronger weaker or the same in a post-apocalyptic World?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Both... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> The Gods use humanity to help define their forms and personalities. Without humanity to inspire them, the line between God and Titan gets blurred. In fact, their real form is just a mass of pure energy until they choose to manifest themselves.<br /> <br /> So without humans around, the Gods would become as powerful as Titans, but also lose their sense of identity in the process.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 07-27-2016, 11:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-28T06:43:56-07:00","id":938798,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/930733-what-are-your-shard-ideas?p=938532#post938532\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Both... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> The Gods use humanity to help define their forms and personalities. Without humanity to inspire them, the line between God and Titan gets blurred. In fact, their real form is just a mass of pure energy until they choose to manifest themselves.<br /> <br /> So without humans around, the Gods would become as powerful as Titans, but also lose their sense of identity in the process.</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting. Also I remember seeing in the blog post gods can radically change after interacting with their people on a crisis,what would happen with the gods who choose to get dirty with their mortal followers to help them in the face of a cataclysm? Could they become wilder,more aggressive to reflect a world that forced their followers to become wilder too?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-28T11:00:22-07:00","id":938952,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/930733-what-are-your-shard-ideas?p=938798#post938798\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Interesting. Also I remember seeing in the blog post gods can radically change after interacting with their people on a crisis,what would happen with the gods who choose to get dirty with their mortal followers to help them in the face of a cataclysm? Could they become wilder,more aggressive to reflect a world that forced their followers to become wilder too?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'm not sure how it works with 2nd edition, but that was the explanation in first edition, I was just re-reading some of it the other day. <br /> <br /> But my guess would be that the Gods could circumvent that possibility by becoming the source of inspiration for mortals instead of the other way around. By which, I mean the Gods give their people some kind of doctrine or religious guidelines to live by. Which, of course, would influence how they perceive the Gods, only it's manipulated in the God's favor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-28T18:18:43-07:00","id":939242,"title":"","content":"Does a fanfic count?<br /> <br /> Because I will work on a crossover with the web serial novel Worm as soon as Origins/Hero comes out.<br /> <br /> Because it's hopeless enough to the point where the idea outlined in the Original Post Apocalyptic Idea (things have gotten so bad the gods have lifted their ban on interfering) works there, too.<br /> <br /> Also because one of the main villainous factions, the Empire 88, are neo-Nazi supervillains. I'd love to see each and every one of them have a long discussion on cultural appropriation and mythological accuracy with Thor's fist (admittedly, more because they profane his culture more than the whole prejudice thing, but that isn't doing them any favors). Except Purity, because the entire arc of her character is that she desperately wants out and maybe even become a (racist, admittedly) hero. But Hookwolf? That wannabe Fenris deserves to have the head of his own armor ripped off and used to beat his stupid tattooes out of his skin.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-28T20:08:36-07:00","id":939303,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/930733-what-are-your-shard-ideas?p=939242#post939242\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does a fanfic count?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would say so, since shards are apparently alternate universes / settings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-07T21:05:26-07:00","id":945917,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/930733-what-are-your-shard-ideas?p=932565#post932565\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Sci-Fi Shard:</b> Megaman-esque world where gods and scions are sophisticated androids, and the Titan of Chaos takes the form of a virus.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I kind of want to see this now! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://vignette2.wikia.nocookie.net/megaman/images/2/2b/AnubisNecromancess.jpg/revision/latest?cb=20080328051432\" target=\"_blank\">Anubis Android</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 08-08-2016, 12:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T17:57:11-07:00","id":954710,"title":"","content":"<b>One of Us:</b> Not only did the Gods not retreat from the World, but they chose to live side by side with mortals. Passing by a lesser immortal on the street is a common day occurrence, while the higher ranking pantheons hold conferences with world leaders to discuss political and militaristic affairs. Mortals feel more comfortable with a God who they can have a face to face conversation with, and now the pantheons are seen from a more relatable point of view. Of course, when magic and monsters become public knowledge, there's obviously going to be some changes to the way the government operates. Specifically, there will be new law enforcement divisions and agencies designed to deal with supernatural threats to society.<br /> <br /> Will your Scion be an agent of these supernatural response divisions, or an antagonist who ends up in their crosshairs?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}